  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE00 Location and Block Plans dated 13.05.2025\rE01 Existing Drawings Floor Plans dated 13.05.2025\rE02 Existing Drawings Elevations dated 13.05.2025\rE03 Existing Drawings Elevations dated 13.05.2025\rE04 Existing Section A-A dated 13.05.2025\rP00 Proposed Location and Block Plans dated 02.06.2025\rP01 Proposed Site Plan dated 02.06.2025\rP02 Proposed Drawings Floor Plans dated 02.06.2025\rP03 Proposed Drawings Elevations dated 02.06.2025\rP04 Proposed Drawings Elevations dated 02.06.2025\rP05 Proposed Section A-A dated 02.06.2025\rP06 Timber Cycle Storage Details dated 02.06.2025 \rP07 Refuse and Recycling Storage Details dated 02.06.2025\rFlood Risk Assessment ref. LE2026680FRA R01 dated June 2026 \rHighway Safety Impact Form\rSuDS Pro Forma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than SEVEN residents at any one time. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Prior to occupation; unless otherwise agreed; cycle parking shall be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\ri) Provision of a minimum of SEVEN long stay cycle parking spaces\r\rii) In an accessible location; the access route to each long stay store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gates [excluding the store door] which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2m.\r\riii) Secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\r\riv) Fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter. \r\rReason: To ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application. \r \rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r"
  ],
